<KCLayout
    title="Property &amp; assessments — KC"
    description="Six county assessors, tax appeals, and what renters can do — across the nine-county Kansas City metro."
>
    <p class="kc-eyebrow">Property</p>
    <h1>Six county assessors, one metro.</h1>
    <p class="kc-lede">
        Property assessment is a county function — and the metro spans nine counties. Each has its
        own assessor, its own valuation timeline, and its own appeal window. If you got a bill or
        a notice you don't understand, find your county here.
    </p>

    <section class="kc-section" aria-labelledby="why">
        <h2 id="why">Why this matters even if you rent</h2>
        <p>
            Landlords pass property tax onto rent. Major mid-year reassessments — like Jackson County's
            in 2023 — pushed rents up across the city. If you rent in a county that just reassessed,
            expect renewal increases. Tenants do not have direct standing in property appeals, but
            community organizing around assessment policy is open.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="kc-section" aria-labelledby="assessors">
        <h2 id="assessors">County assessors</h2>

        <h3>Missouri (5)</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Jackson County:</strong> <a href="tel:816-881-3530">816-881-3530</a> · <a href="https://www.jacksongov.org/government/departments/assessment" rel="noopener noreferrer">jacksongov.org</a> · reassessment every 2 years (odd years)</li>
            <li><strong>Clay County:</strong> <a href="tel:816-407-3500">816-407-3500</a> · <a href="https://www.claycountymo.gov/departments/assessor" rel="noopener noreferrer">claycountymo.gov</a></li>
            <li><strong>Platte County:</strong> <a href="tel:816-858-3303">816-858-3303</a> · <a href="https://www.plattecountymo.gov/200/Assessor" rel="noopener noreferrer">plattecountymo.gov</a></li>
            <li><strong>Cass County:</strong> <a href="tel:816-380-8400">816-380-8400</a></li>
            <li><strong>Ray County:</strong> <a href="tel:816-776-2676">816-776-2676</a></li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Kansas (4)</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Wyandotte County / UG:</strong> <a href="tel:913-573-2885">913-573-2885</a> · <a href="https://www.wycokck.org/Departments/Appraisers-Office" rel="noopener noreferrer">wycokck.org</a></li>
            <li><strong>Johnson County:</strong> <a href="tel:913-715-9000">913-715-9000</a> · <a href="https://www.jocogov.org/dept/appraiser" rel="noopener noreferrer">jocogov.org</a></li>
            <li><strong>Leavenworth County:</strong> <a href="tel:913-684-1030">913-684-1030</a></li>
            <li><strong>Miami County:</strong> <a href="tel:913-294-4045">913-294-4045</a></li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="kc-section" aria-labelledby="appeals">
        <h2 id="appeals">Appealing your assessment</h2>
        <p>
            Each county has a window — typically 30-45 days from when the notice goes out. Miss the
            window and you wait until next cycle. The process:
        </p>
        <ol>
            <li>Read the assessment notice carefully. Look for the "appeal deadline" and the "value used."</li>
            <li>Gather comparable sales (sometimes the county portal has these; otherwise pull from Zillow, Redfin, or the MLS via a realtor).</li>
            <li>File an informal appeal with the assessor (usually a form online).</li>
            <li>If denied, file a formal appeal with the County Board of Equalization (MO) or County Appraiser Hearing (KS).</li>
            <li>If still denied, you can appeal to the State Tax Commission (MO) or BOTA (KS).</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
            In Jackson County after the 2023 reassessment, organized appeal clinics ran in community
            spaces. The Beacon, KC Tenants, and several legal aid groups have hosted these. Watch for
            them in years when reassessments hit.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="kc-section" aria-labelledby="exemptions">
        <h2 id="exemptions">Homestead, senior, veteran exemptions</h2>
        <p>
            Each state has its own:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Missouri:</strong> Property Tax Credit (PTC, the "circuit breaker") — refund for low-income elderly + disabled homeowners and renters. File Form MO-PTC. <a href="https://dor.mo.gov/personal/ptc/" rel="noopener noreferrer">dor.mo.gov/ptc</a></li>
            <li><strong>Missouri Senior Property Tax Freeze:</strong> 2024+ — each county opted in separately. Check your county.</li>
            <li><strong>Kansas:</strong> Homestead Refund (file Form K-40H). For low-income, elderly, disabled, or veteran. <a href="https://www.ksrevenue.gov/perstaxtypeshs.html" rel="noopener noreferrer">ksrevenue.gov</a></li>
            <li><strong>Kansas SAFESR:</strong> additional refund for seniors 65+.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="kc-section" aria-labelledby="renter">
        <h2 id="renter">If you rent</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>MO renters</strong> may qualify for the Property Tax Credit (PTC) if low-income.</li>
            <li><strong>KS renters</strong> can claim a portion of rent on the Homestead Refund.</li>
            <li><strong>KCMO Tenant Bill of Rights</strong> requires landlords to provide certain disclosures and protects against retaliation. Enforcement: 816-513-3200.</li>
            <li><strong>Security deposit limits:</strong> MO — max 2 months' rent. KS — max 1 month (unfurnished) or 1.5 months (furnished).</li>
            <li><strong>Required notice for rent increase:</strong> MO — 30 days for month-to-month. KS — 30 days.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            For tenant defense, see <a href="/kc/legal">legal</a> and <a href="/kc/housing">housing</a>.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="kc-section" aria-labelledby="records">
        <h2 id="records">Property records (the deed, who owns it)</h2>
        <p>
            County recorders / register of deeds have the actual ownership records. If you want to know
            who owns a property:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Jackson MO Recorder of Deeds:</strong> <a href="https://www.jacksongov.org/recorder" rel="noopener noreferrer">jacksongov.org/recorder</a> · online search</li>
            <li><strong>Wyandotte KS Register of Deeds:</strong> <a href="https://www.wycokck.org/Departments/Register-of-Deeds" rel="noopener noreferrer">wycokck.org</a></li>
            <li><strong>Johnson KS Register of Deeds:</strong> <a href="https://www.jocogov.org/dept/register-deeds" rel="noopener noreferrer">jocogov.org</a></li>
            <li><strong>Other counties:</strong> see county sites listed in <a href="/kc/government">government</a></li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</KCLayout>
